ions⠀of⠀what⠀happened,⠀and⠀private⠀speculation.⠀Each⠀digression⠀returns⠀with⠀new⠀pressure⠀on⠀the⠀present⠀relationship:⠀a⠀rumor⠀about⠀the⠀offense,⠀a⠀half-remembered⠀apology,⠀or⠀a⠀detail⠀of⠀the⠀scene⠀can⠀become⠀the⠀hinge⠀that⠀brings⠀the⠀narrator⠀back⠀to⠀what⠀they⠀still⠀cannot⠀say⠀or⠀ask.\n\nMake⠀emotional⠀strain⠀alter⠀the⠀actual⠀movement⠀of⠀a⠀conversation.⠀Let⠀a⠀character⠀begin⠀a⠀practical⠀question⠀about⠀evidence,⠀money,⠀or⠀loyalty⠀and⠀then⠀swerve⠀into⠀accusation,⠀need,⠀or⠀withheld⠀admission.⠀The⠀narrator⠀may⠀notice⠀the⠀swerve⠀without⠀resolving⠀it.⠀When⠀comfort⠀appears,⠀keep⠀it⠀partial⠀or⠀awkward:⠀someone⠀may⠀offer⠀help⠀while⠀refusing⠀the⠀closeness⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀wants,⠀or⠀may⠀say⠀the⠀right⠀practical⠀thing⠀and⠀still⠀leave⠀the⠀deeper⠀injury⠀untouched.⠀Warmth⠀and⠀pain⠀can⠀occupy⠀the⠀same⠀exchange.\n\nUse⠀the⠀Rushdie⠀profile's⠀associative⠀range⠀to⠀show⠀how⠀a⠀private⠀hurt⠀becomes⠀entangled⠀with⠀public⠀story.⠀A⠀witness's⠀account,⠀a⠀neighborhood⠀version⠀of⠀the⠀offense,⠀or⠀a⠀remembered⠀cultural⠀reference⠀can⠀supply⠀language⠀the⠀characters⠀use⠀to⠀avoid⠀or⠀approach⠀what⠀they⠀feel.⠀Do⠀not⠀let⠀that⠀public⠀material⠀replace⠀the⠀private⠀interiority;⠀let⠀it⠀give⠀the⠀narrator⠀a⠀way⠀to⠀misname,⠀exaggerate,⠀or⠀delay⠀the⠀admission⠀that⠀matters.⠀The⠀turbulent⠀feeling⠀should⠀emerge⠀from⠀the⠀narrator's⠀specific⠀diction⠀and⠀digressive⠀habits,⠀not⠀from⠀a⠀repeated⠀vocabulary⠀of⠀anguish.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀crime's⠀practical⠀stakes⠀legible.⠀The⠀offense⠀still⠀has⠀preparation,⠀consequences,⠀evidence,⠀or⠀pursuit,⠀and⠀the⠀characters⠀still⠀have⠀incentives⠀they⠀may⠀conceal.⠀Emotional⠀exposure⠀does⠀not⠀erase⠀those⠀stakes;⠀it⠀complicates⠀them.⠀A⠀character⠀can⠀withhold⠀a⠀fact⠀because⠀apology⠀feels⠀impossible,⠀or⠀confess⠀a⠀lesser⠀fault⠀to⠀avoid⠀a⠀greater⠀one.⠀Let⠀the⠀reader⠀see⠀the⠀cost⠀of⠀returning⠀to⠀the⠀difficult⠀relationship⠀wherever⠀the⠀scene⠀actually⠀takes⠀it.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{trim}}{{/if}}"
